```

- **`kebabCase`** comes from `es-toolkit`. It matched lodash on all sampled inputs.
- **`keyBy`** uses es-toolkit's function form, which needs a one-line adapter `(row) => row.name` because the call shape differs from lodash's property shorthand. Using es-toolkit's compat `keyBy` with `'name'` would have kept the shape but grown the bundle to 3381 bytes, so I rejected it.
- **`toNumber`** comes from `es-toolkit/compat`, because the main `es-toolkit` entry does not export it. The compat version matched lodash on every sampled input, including `9x80`, `87x47e .`, hex, and exponent forms.
- Nothing was installed. I did not touch `src/module.ts`.

